A||N||12||87ECO5||Best product for cleaning white-lettered tires||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||05-29-2001||08:28 AM||||The white letters on my tires are so dirty, you can't even see them.<P>What's a good product to use to clean them?  I've used Ajax and a scrub brush but it leaves a white residue on the tire.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||05-29-2001||08:41 AM||||Try "Mean Green". The only place I've ever seen it is Dollar General.<BR>Read the label. I think it says not to use it on aluminum.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||05-29-2001||09:07 AM||||Westley's whitewall cleaner. You can find it in any auto parts and most department stores. I use that to knock brake dust off my wheels too. It's a little on the harsh side tho - make sure it doesn't dry before you scrub/hose it off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-29-2001||09:39 AM||||When I had raised white letters on my old tires I just used a small stainless steel wire brush and the car soap. Caution using chemicals on aluminum wheels, some will corrode the aluminum if there are chips in the clearcoat. Check the label of the product you buy. I think Eagle1 makes something for the letters that's not harmful to the aluminum. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||kslish||05-29-2001||02:34 PM||||Westley's Bleach-White.  That's what I use on mine.  Spray it on, a little scrubbing with an old toothbrush, rinse it ALL off (and don't let it drip and dry on any aluminum) and the letters look brand new.  I follow with a coat of No-Touch spray-on Tire Care....it provides a coating to keep the letters cleaner a little longer.<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||05-29-2001||04:43 PM||||I always just soaked them down with 409 or Fantastic, then used a brass brush on them. Left white white, and the black nice and clean black (not shiny) Most of those tire dressings turn the letters off white.||||reg||1
Z||000006||saleenfiero||05-29-2001||04:45 PM||||What's wrong with those blue pot scrubber pads?  I use them all the time and my friend though I had covered the lettering in wite-out because it was so intense.||||reg||10
Z||000007||Taijiguy||05-29-2001||05:10 PM||||My vote also goes to Westley's Bleche White. It kicks butt.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rex||05-29-2001||10:24 PM||||Westleys' Bleach White requires no scrubbing<BR>at the car wash. Spray it on just prior to starting the wash, give it a few minutes and hold the wand a couple inches from the white letters and presto! chango! new lookin tires again.The tires require slight scrubbing in the drive way where hand washing is done. And I didn't get paid to say this.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||05-29-2001||10:35 PM||||WESTLEY'S BLEACH WHITE!!!  I used it on my tires, my white convertible top (on the VW), my headliner, my.....*fades into oblivion*<P>It's good!  Got my white convertible top clean everytime, whether I was trying to clean bird droppings, rotten cherries, mudstains, tree pitch, or just grime.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||10
Z||000010||fiero56||05-30-2001||12:27 AM||||I tried the purple Meguiars cleaner that comes in a spray bottle this past weekend on mine. Sprayed the letters down, and scrubbed 'em with my wheel brush. They look better than they have since I bought the car.||||reg||1
Z||000011||danny boy||05-31-2001||10:51 PM|||| I, and most of my Family Before me, swear by Bleach white. The stuff cleans all kinds of stuff. <BR>Greased Lightneng is my new favorite, though. It works just as good on twice as many things and is even biodegradeable for the Enviornmentally friendly. Be careful, it'll eat the skin right off your hands!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Nashco||05-31-2001||11:40 PM||||LMAO danny boy!!!  How the hell did they get you to believe that...that's some damn smooth sales! "...and is even biodegradeable for the environmentally friendly,"  followed right up with, "Be careful, it'll eat the skin right off your hands!"<P>Now, I'm not a chemical engineer, but if it'll make your hands raw, won't it pretty much F up most any living cells easily?<P>LOL...seriously, come on!  Most any of these chemicals are pretty nasty, but at least they don't claim to be good for the environment.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
